                <pb facs="1058" n="938" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg938"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bowen to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen reports the answer of the Venezuelan Government just received. It is
                    an absolute refusal to comply with Department’s request to withdraw receiver and
                    to return the property to the company. The answer states that Venezuelan
                    Government leaves the decision entirely to the court; that the United States
                    could logically reserve all rights and undertake diplomatic intervention only
                    after the decision of the court is rendered.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
